0, "output_tail": "Now verify against a real local HTTP server.\n`WeatherClient.get` now retries when the server returns 503: up to 3 attempts total, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them. The 3 new tests pass.\n\n**How it behaves** (`weather.py`):\n- It catches the HTTP error that `urllib` raises for a 503 and retries.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller as usual.\n- Any other HTTP error (500, 404, etc.) is raised immediately with no retry.\n- Network errors (timeouts, refused connections) are also not retried, since you only asked for 503s.\n- The attempt count and wait time are class attributes, `max_attempts = 3` and `backoff_base = 0.5`, so they can be changed per instance.\n\n**Tests:** I added `test_weather.py`, which runs a real local HTTP server rather than mocks, with warnings treated as errors. It checks three cases:\n- Two 503s then a 200: returns the data after 3 requests.\n- 503 every time: raises the 503 after exactly 3 requests.\n- A 500: raises at once after 1 request.\n\nTo keep the tests fast they set `backoff_base` to 0.01, so the real 0.5s/1s timing isn't measured by any test.\n\nRe-run with `python3 -m unittest -v test_weather`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69822, "requests_cache_write": 147181, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7950254, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 2255, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 6, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:23.984848+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 28.873, "t_checker_s": 2.385, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "non